{"id":139,"title":"Coastal Fish in Shinnecock Memory","slug":"coastal-fish","summary":"The catalogue describes returning alewives as a sign of spring and remembers their use in planting. Seasonal fish movements connected the water with work in gardens.","content":"<section data-source-section=\"shinnecock-elders-2014\"><h2>Knowledge recorded by Shinnecock elders in 2014</h2><h3>Alewives</h3><p>The catalogue describes returning alewives as a sign of spring and remembers their use in planting. Seasonal fish movements connected the water with work in gardens.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-1\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 2. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=2\">1</a></sup></p><h4>Places named in the catalogue</h4><p>Heady Crick; <a href=\"#listing/conscience-point\">Conscience Point</a>; Turtle Pond.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-1\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 2. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=2\">1</a></sup></p><h3>Atlantic salmon in elders’ memories</h3><p>Elders remembered catching fish they called salmon on the ocean side when they were young. They also recalled older fishers going to Conscience Point when shad moved upstream.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-1\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 2. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=2\">1</a></sup></p><h4>Places named in the catalogue</h4><p><a href=\"#listing/montaukett-ancestral-land\">Montauk</a>; Long Island Sound; Atlantic Ocean; <a href=\"#listing/conscience-point\">Conscience Point</a>.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-1\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 2. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=2\">1</a></sup></p><h3>Northern puffer / blowfish</h3><p>The catalogue remembers blowfish as food and names Shinnecock Bay, the Atlantic Ocean, and the Mecox Bay area, showing how fishing knowledge spanned protected bays and the ocean shore.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-1\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 2. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=2\">1</a></sup></p><h4>Places named in the catalogue</h4><p><a href=\"#listing/shinnecock-ancestral-land\">Shinnecock Bay</a>; Atlantic Ocean; <a href=\"#listing/mecox-bridgehampton\">Mecox Bay</a>.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-1\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 2. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=2\">1</a></sup></p><h3>Bluefish</h3><p>The catalogue follows bluefish from spring into late fall and describes the bays as feeding and breeding waters. Its attention to season and water conditions records knowledge built through repeated fishing.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-1\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 2. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=2\">1</a></sup></p><h4>Places named in the catalogue</h4><p>Heady Crick; Great South Bay; <a href=\"#listing/shinnecock-ancestral-land\">Shinnecock Bay</a>; <a href=\"#listing/pahquahkossit\">Wading River bays</a>; Atlantic Ocean; Long Island Sound.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-1\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 2. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=2\">1</a></sup></p><h3>Dogfish and sharks</h3><p>The catalogue describes smooth dogfish in shallow bays and other inshore waters, moving north in spring and south in autumn. Nurse sharks and sand sharks are listed alongside dogfish as separate names.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-1\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 2. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=2\">1</a></sup></p><h4>Places named in the catalogue</h4><p><a href=\"#listing/shinnecock-ancestral-land\">Shinnecock waters</a>.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-1\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 2. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=2\">1</a></sup></p><h3>Flounder</h3><p>The elders’ catalogue identifies the southern bay bottoms with seasonal flounder fishing. The entry treats the bay floor as a living part of the community’s food landscape.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-2\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 3. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=3\">2</a></sup></p><h4>Places named in the catalogue</h4><p>Atlantic Ocean; Long Island Sound; <a href=\"#listing/pahquahkossit\">Wading River bays</a>.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-2\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 3. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=3\">2</a></sup></p><h3>Sea robins</h3><p>Sea robins are remembered for striking fins, sounds, and their place in Shinnecock meals. The catalogue records several English nicknames and associates them with waters also used by weakfish and fluke.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-2\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 3. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=3\">2</a></sup></p><h4>Places named in the catalogue</h4><p>Long Island waters.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-2\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 3. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=3\">2</a></sup></p><h3>American shad</h3><p>The catalogue places shad in both food and planting traditions. Fish arriving in spring are part of a seasonal relationship also recalled in the shadbush entry, where flowering signaled the time to prepare for shad fishing.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-2\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 3. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=3\">2</a></sup></p><h4>Places named in the catalogue</h4><p><a href=\"#listing/pahquahkossit\">Wading River bays</a>; South Shore waterways; Atlantic Ocean.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-2\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 3. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=3\">2</a></sup></p><h3>Striped bass and other bass names</h3><p>The catalogue lists striped bass as a familiar fish of local waterways and records white or silver bass in the same row.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-2\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 3. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=3\">2</a></sup></p><h4>Places named in the catalogue</h4><p>Long Island waters.<sup class=\"article-footnote\"><a href=\"#nli-ref-201520283-2\" title=\"Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF p. 3. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.\" data-source-url=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=3\">2</a></sup></p><h3>Page references</h3><p>The Shinnecock Environmental Department compiled this catalogue from elders’ memories and community resource knowledge in 2014. Food and medicine appear here as historical knowledge; safe identification and treatment require current guidance.</p><p><a href=\"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf#page=2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Shinnecock Environmental Department, Natural Resources Identified by Shinnecock Elders, April 4, 2014, PDF pp. 2–3. Page numbers count the cover as PDF page 1.</a></p><p><a href=\"#wiki/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014\">Explore the full resource and place directory</a> · <a href=\"#wiki/language\">Algonquian Language</a> · <a href=\"#wiki/native-plants\">Native Plants</a></p></section>","why_this_matters":null,"source_url":"https://nativelongisland.com/assets/documents/shinnecock-elders-natural-resources-2014.pdf","activity_update_date":null,"activity_update_summary":null,"last_reviewed":"2026-09-20T00:00:00","lastmod":null,"imported_at":"2026-05-12T19:50:01.281Z"}